  "sourceNotes": "Sundubu jjigae, meaning 'soft tofu stew', is a staple of Korean home cooking and is especially popular in the Gyeonggi region around Seoul. The dish gained international attention through the chain Soon Tofu, which popularised the Los Angeles Korean-American version. The home version is simpler and more broth-forward than restaurant styles.",
