      "slug": "gochugaru",
      "term": "Gochugaru",
      "definition": "Korean red chilli flakes made from sun-dried red chillies. They are coarser and less fiery than most chilli powders and have a slightly fruity, smoky flavour. Gochugaru is used in kimchi, stews, and seasoning pastes across Korean cooking."
    },
    {
      "slug": "silken-tofu",
      "term": "Silken tofu",
      "definition": "A very soft, custard-like form of tofu that breaks apart easily. It is not pressed, so it retains all the water from the curdling process. It is suited to soups and stews where it absorbs the surrounding broth."
    }
  ],
