  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sundubu jjigae takes 25 minutes and serves 2. It is one of the simplest Korean stews to cook. The heat comes from "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "gochugaru",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "gochugaru"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and the main component is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "silken tofu",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "silken-tofu"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", which soaks up the spicy broth. An egg cracked in at the end finishes the dish."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The key step is blooming the gochugaru in oil first. This draws out its colour and flavour before the liquid goes in. Do not skip this step. Thirty seconds in a little sesame oil transforms the chilli from raw and dusty to rich and fragrant."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
